Package: scholararcs
Title: Citation Arcs for Any Researcher
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Aaron", "Erlich", email = "aaron.erlich@mcgill.ca", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Draws three views of a researcher's citation record: cumulative
    citations in calendar time, cumulative citations aligned on each paper's
    publication year, and the per-year arc that shows when papers actually
    peaked. Papers are coloured by the kind of venue that published them,
    tiered automatically within the author's own field and overridable by hand.
    Reads from OpenAlex by default, which works anywhere; a Google Scholar
    backend is available when the app is run locally.
